  42:     - Exactly two red pixels share one row or one column; this aligned pair defines the spine segment.
  43:     - Every other red pixel lies within the span of that spine along the perpendicular direction.
  44: 
  45:     Rule
  46:     - Paint the background cells between the aligned red pair green, preserving the red endpoints.
  47:     - If the spine is horizontal, draw a vertical green segment from each other red pixel to the spine.
  48:     - If the spine is vertical, draw a horizontal green segment from each other red pixel to the spine.
  49: 
  50:     Key insight
  51:     - The only repeated row or column among the red pixels is the connector trunk; all remaining pixels attach to it perpendicularly.
  52:     """
  53:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
  54:     assert g.ndim == 2, "expected a 2D grid"
  55: 
  56:     bg = get_bg(g)
  57:     assert bg == Color.BACKGROUND, "expected black background"
  58:     assert set(colors_present(g)) == {Color.BACKGROUND, Color.RED}, "expected only black background and red controls"
  59: 
  60:     red_coords = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(g == Color.RED)]
